[profiles.guide]
notes = '''Hold {select} and {start} together to pause the gyro while you reposition the controller. Tilting the controller moves the pointer, as a fine pointer next to the right stick {rs}.
The right stick {rs} moves the pointer and the left stick {ls} pans the camera. {rt} or {south} clicks; hold {lt} and move the right stick {rs} to turn and tilt the camera. {up} and {down} zoom, {left} and {right} turn the camera.
Hold {lb} and press the {dpad} for the move tools: up moves, right is the advanced move, down deletes and left switches the freelook camera.
{west} turns what you're placing a quarter; hold it and move the pointer to turn it freely. Hold {north} and move the pointer up or down to change its height, {r3} resets it. Hold {rb} for Ctrl. {l3} switches angle snap.
{east} cancels and deselects, {start} is the menu. The park's screens and build categories have no keys we could confirm: point at them on the toolbar.
Keys are the game's defaults from its v1.0 keybind list and players' notes, not read from an install; the move tools, delete and freelook are assumed to match Planet Zoo's. If one is off, check Settings → Controls. The Console Edition's rebuilt interface can't be copied, so this follows the PC keys. Naming a ride or the park: {guide} + {west} opens the on-screen keyboard.'''

